speechtext:
On the order for notices of motions:
Whereas the minister in charge of the Department of External Affairs has been up to the present date the prime minister of the day;
And whereas the said department has developed and grown in size a.nd importance to the point where the appointment of a full-time minister is essential in the public interest;
And whereas Canada's responsibilities abroad require ever more frequently the attendance of the appropriate cabinet minister at international gatherings outside Canada;
Therefore, be it resolved that in the opinion of this house the government should consider immediately the advisability of appointing a minister of the crown whose duties shall be solely concerned with external affairs.
